{
 "about": "Texts with `<!-->`, `<!--->` or `<?>` before a part that GitHub hides and that holds a `-->` or a `?>`: a quoted value of a tag, a tag over rows, the content of a `video`, an `rp` or a `relative-time`, a void tag in `svg` or `math`, a link reference definition, a title, a cell, an info string, a drawing and math; as a block, three spaces in, below a paragraph, in a quote, a list item, a heading and a cell, and inline; and the forms inside a `div`, `details`, a table, `pre`, `svg`, `math`, `script`, `style`, a longer comment, a value, a fence and a code span. Each with the marker words that GitHub's renderer (gh api -X POST markdown with mode gfm, 2026-11-23) shows and hides, as a headless Chrome read the page; GitHub's script draws a date in place of a relative-time, and a diagram or transparent math in place of their source.",
